 "_doc": "Sebata-style 'TAX INVOICE / STATEMENT OF ACCOUNT' (two prints: one with 'Account Number:' on its own line, one with 'Account / Number:' split around the account date). A METER READINGS table (meter no., type, old/new reading, flag, consumption, levied amount, reading dates) precedes ACCOUNT DETAILS (date, code, description, units @ tariff, value EX VAT); VAT is one whole-bill line. Electricity lines carry codes nnEnnn ('INTEREST nnEnnn ...' lines are interest, not counted). On all 10 bills the electricity meter is idle (old = new reading, 0 kWh, levied 0.00) and only 'BASIC - COMMERCIAL THREE PHASE' is charged, so standard_r stays blank and other_r = total. FINGERPRINT: municipal VAT number + name/domain. total_ex_vat_r = sum of nnEnnn line values; identity gam_check_r = units x tariff of the basic line (mul) + any other nnEnnn line - independent of the printed value column for the basic charge. One bill is OCR (reads cleanly). Checked on 10 bills.",
